  "definition": "Herpes-simplex encephalitis is a serious viral illness in which herpes simplex virus infects the brain. It can cause fever, headache, vomiting, seizures, and psychiatric symptoms, with type 1 more often affecting adults and type 2 more often affecting newborns.",
